  "question": {
    "text": "The potential at a point $x$ (measured in $\\mu \\mathrm{m}$ ) due to some charges situated on the $\\mathrm{x}$-axis is given by $\\mathrm{V(x)=20 /\\left(x^2-4\\right)} \\mathrm{~Volts}$. The electric field $\\mathrm{E}$ at $\\mathrm{x=4 ~\\mu m}$ is given by"
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "text": "\n$5 / 3 \\mathrm{~Volt}/$ $\\mu \\mathrm{m}$ and in the $-ve$ $x$ direction\n",
      "is_correct": false
    },
    {
      "text": "\n$5 / 3 \\mathrm{~Volt}/$ $\\mu \\mathrm{m}$ and in the $+ve$ $x$ direction.\n",
      "is_correct": false
    },
    {
      "text": "\n$10 / 9 \\mathrm{~Volt} / \\mu \\mathrm{m}$ and in the $-ve$ $x$ direction\n",
      "is_correct": false
    },
    {
      "text": "\n$10 / 9 \\mathrm{~Volt} / \\mu \\mathrm{m}$ and in the $+ve$ $x$ direction.",
      "is_correct": true
    }
  ],
  "correct_answer": [
    "D"
  ],
  "solution": {
    "text": "$\\mathrm{V_x=\\frac{20}{x^2-4}}$\n$\\mathrm{E=-\\frac{d V}{d x}=\\frac{20}{\\left(x^2-4\\right)^2}(2 x-0)=\\frac{160}{144}=\\frac{10}{9}}$"
  }
}